+
+
+## Windows storage requirements and controller validation
+
+The optional service lazily loads `windows_privacy.py`. Stock-disabled loads do
+not import Win32. The verifier derives the user SID from the process token and
+requires the private directory, enrollment/grant files, database and journal to
+be owned by that user, LocalSystem or built-in Administrators. These are the
+same three identities permitted in nonzero effective allow ACEs. Ownership is
+checked from the opened object against explicit SIDs, never an account name,
+environment variable or arbitrary default token owner. Administrators-owned
+objects are within this existing local trust boundary; ownership does not
+excuse a broad or malformed DACL. On the leaf directory this also applies
+to inheritable/inherit-only permissions, so new database/journal files cannot
+inherit outsider access. Explicit denies do not excuse a broad allow.
+
+Each existing ancestor through the filesystem root is separately inspected.
+Read/list/traverse and create-sibling rights alone are permitted there. Outsider
+DELETE, DELETE_CHILD, WRITE_DAC, WRITE_OWNER, write-EA or write-attributes rights
+are refused. Ancestor ownership must also be the process user, SYSTEM or built-in
+Administrators, with one exact ancestor-owner exception: Windows Modules Installer
+(TrustedInstaller), SID
+`S-1-5-80-956008885-3418522649-1831038044-1853292631-2271478464`.
+This accounts for standard system-drive ownership. It grants no new effective ACE
+permission and does not permit that SID to own or receive permissions on private
+leaves. Other service SIDs, near-matching SIDs and localized names confer no trust.
+Inherit-only ancestor ACEs do not confer rights on the pinned existing component;
+every descendant is independently inspected, including the private leaf's future
+inheritance. No existing/system ACL is repaired and no administrator bypass or
+assume-safe option exists.
+
+Only local fixed NTFS volumes and ordinary absolute DOS paths up to 240 characters
+are supported. Reparse points/junctions, multiple file hardlinks, streams, UNC,
+SUBST/alias paths, missing/null DACLs, conditional/object/unknown ACEs, unknown
+access bits and unresolved native queries are refused. Ordinary standard allow
+and deny ACEs are parsed with bounded counts and lengths. Future unsupported
+layouts require review, not an automatic exception.
+
+Authority reads pin every ancestor against rename and open the leaf without
+reparse following, denying write/delete sharing. Validation and bounded reads
+use that same handle. Grant shape, enrollment completeness, current key comparison
+and current-grant checks remain mandatory. A failed read never becomes an empty
+allowlist. Initial stock registry loading/writing stays unchanged; optional
+snapshot reads add the native boundary and retain the persistent incomplete marker.
+
+SQLite operations pin the private directory and database. Preexisting journals
+are inspected before opening SQLite; WAL/SHM state is unsupported and refused.
+Windows never chmods or rewrites an existing object's ACL. Creation inherits the
+checked private directory, and the newly created database is inspected. Every
+transaction writes the unchanged `user_version` to force a real rollback journal,
+then inspects its descriptor before payload code runs and again before commit.
+The journal may contain existing page data before its inspection, so directory
+inheritance is checked first; a later change by the current user or an administrator
+is within the stated trusted boundary. FULL durability, DELETE mode, size limits,
+identity/dedup, expiry and ACK behavior remain unchanged. An unsafe or failed check
+rolls back and raises a concise setup/service failure; it does not repair storage.
+
+Run the standalone synthetic fixture with the **actual gateway interpreter** from
+an extracted private source bundle; no package installation is needed:
+
+```powershell
+& $GatewayPython -I -W error .\tests\windows_privacy_native.py --parent $OwnedTestParent --receipt $NewReceiptPath
+if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Windows relay native privacy gate failed" }
+```
+
+The controller selects an existing local parent and a new private receipt path.
+Only a fresh randomly named child is modified and removed in `finally`. No live
+registry, service, endpoint, device, provider, account or installed permission is
+touched. The parent must satisfy the production ancestor policy. It need not be traversable
+by the test's restricted token: the probe uses one pinned directory handle scoped
+to the new fixture. Existing private user-home ancestry is not traversed by its
+restricted file opens. Unsafe temporary-directory ancestors remain unsupported;
+no existing/system ancestor ACL may be changed to accommodate the fixture.
+
+The runner exercises native private read/size checks, effective/inherited/null
+DACL denial, ancestor replacement, hardlinks/streams, junctions, same-object reads
+and replacement refusal, enrollment rotation with independent watch/phone keys,
+new database/active journal descriptors, rollback, restart/dedup/ACK and preserved
+unsafe bytes. Symlink creation may skip only when the OS refuses its privilege;
+junction/hardlink and every other mandatory check must pass. Injected native-query
+failure tests are identified separately from kernel access evidence.
+
+The negative access probe is a disposable subprocess using a restricted version
+of the same user's token, **not** a second account. Administrators is deny-only
+when present, Everyone is the sole restricting SID, and every privilege is disabled
+and checked, including traverse bypass. Before impersonation it opens only a
+new fixture-directory handle, with traversal/metadata rights and no delete sharing.
+Both files are siblings there. The directory's non-inheriting Everyone read/traverse
+ACE is part of fresh synthetic fixture creation; the private file's DACL remains
+user/SYSTEM/Administrators only. Existing parents and private DACLs are not relaxed.
+
+After impersonation, test-only `NtCreateFile` opens each single-component name
+relative to that same pinned handle, with identical read rights and synchronous,
+non-directory, no-reparse-follow options. Neither file is preopened. The control
+must return its expected bytes; the private open must return exact
+`STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED` (`0xC0000022`). Missing-file, path, pending or other native
+errors cannot satisfy the negative assertion. Every handle is closed; impersonation
+is reverted in `finally` before releasing the directory handle, and failed reversion
+terminates the disposable child. No privilege is enabled.
+
+This tests kernel enforcement of the private **file DACL** when the constrained
+caller is given a directory handle. It does not claim that a second account can
+traverse existing user-home ancestry. Production root-to-leaf privacy is checked
+separately, including a successful private-directory precondition before each native
+method and positive reads before the reparse/hardlink/broad-DACL negative fixtures.
+These preconditions prevent an unrelated ancestor failure from masquerading as a
+successful leaf denial. The source-bound controller rerun on both architectures
+remains mandatory.
+
+Each receipt records OS, interpreter/bitness, source hashes, the process user SID,
+and queried owner SIDs/classes for the fixture parent/root, each private test
+directory, database and active journal. Owner classes are derived from each
+opened object rather than assumed to match TokenUser. Assertions, skip reasons
+and cleanup are also recorded. Receipts contain local identity/path details
+and must remain private. A missing/failed native run blocks that host's activation.
+Controller review of both required hosts precedes export, installation, capability
+advertisement or restart. Running this fixture never enables the service.
+
+Native contracts: [CreateFileW and sharing](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-createfilew),
+[GetSecurityInfo ownership and allocation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/aclapi/nf-aclapi-getsecurityinfo),
+[file access masks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/file-access-rights-constants),
+[handle volume inspection](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-getvolumeinformationbyhandlew),
+and [restricted tokens](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/securitybaseapi/nf-securitybaseapi-createrestrictedtoken).
+
+
+The fixture's native relative-open ABI follows [NtCreateFile](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winternl/nf-winternl-ntcreatefile),
+[OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/ntdef/ns-ntdef-_object_attributes),
+[UNICODE_STRING](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/ntdef/ns-ntdef-_unicode_string),
+and [IO_STATUS_BLOCK](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/wdm/ns-wdm-_io_status_block).
+The production module does not use the test-only NtCreateFile interface.
